From ead31c699bd4717eb21059f1d7fe2a8ec54ec8e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:59:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): push session transcript deltas into the tail
 cache (sessions.moved) [daveey]

The background prefetcher learned a session moved from the 5 s hub listing poll,
whose activity/message_count the hub holds for up to 30 s, and then refetched the
latest page at most once per 30 s: an open found newer messages than its cache
paint in 11 of 16 opens.

Gateway: a new global `sessions.moved` change-watcher event, at most once a
second and only when message rows were added, naming each moved session
{id, profile, message_count, activity, last_message_id, parent_session_id}.
Its signature is each watched store's MAX(messages.id) behind the kept
observer's commit key (one PRAGMA while idle); the payload reads the id range
since the last frame, so a floored window loses nothing. Added to the gateway
contract (events.py, regenerated TS/OpenRPC).

REST: `GET /api/sessions/{id}/messages?after_id=N[&limit]` returns the live
display rows after row N (bounded, default 200, max 500) plus
delta.{anchor_found, has_more, transcript_revision}, read revision-first.

Desktop: the renderer forwards every socket's sessions.moved to main
(store/transcript-push.ts); the prefetcher fetches only the rows after each
tracked session's cached tail, one fetch in flight + one queued per session,
no 30 s throttle, and falls back to the latest page when the delta does not
line up (anchor row gone, gap, rotation, in-place rewrite since the last full
page, cache moved under the delta, older core without the route). The listing
pass becomes a 60 s safety net for a gateway that pushes (5 s otherwise); an
unknown moved session asks for an early listing pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
